feat(vox-gui): implement console input editor, discovery rail, terminal, and agent strip
scale: ~437 lines across 8 files [L]

- `InputEditor.tsx`: Adds a console prompt component with ghost text for catalog suggestions, allowing Tab/Right Arrow to accept and Enter to submit. It debounces user input to fetch suggestions via `discoverySuggest`.
- `TerminalTab.tsx`: Implements a PTY-backed terminal using xterm.js. It spawns a PTY on mount, streams output, and forwards interactive keystrokes and parent-submitted lines to the backend via `ptySpawn`, `ptyWrite`, `listenPtyOutput`, and `listenPtyExit`.
- `DiscoveryRail.tsx`: Creates a right-hand rail that resolves the active action ID to its help text using `discoveryHelp` and records a "seen" exposure with dwell via `discoveryRecord`.
- `AgentStrip.tsx`: Introduces a persistent strip displaying live agent chips, with data mapped from `vox://orch-status`. Clicking a chip triggers an `onOpen` event.
- `TerminalTab.test.tsx`: Adds Vitest tests for `TerminalTab`, verifying PTY spawning and line writing.
- `DiscoveryRail.test.tsx`: Adds Vitest tests for `DiscoveryRail`, confirming help rendering and "seen" exposure recording.
- `InputEditor.test.tsx`: Adds Vitest tests for `InputEditor`.
- `AgentStrip.test.tsx`: Adds Vitest tests for `AgentStrip`.

